# MCP Git path encoding

Use these rules for the `repo_path` argument in MCP Git commands.

## Required format

```
C:/Users/path/to/repo    # correct
```

- Absolute path with drive letter on Windows.
- Forward slashes (`/`), not backslashes.
- No URL encoding (`%3A` for `:`).
- No duplicate drive letters (`C:\c%3A\...`).
- No leading slash before the drive letter.

## Forbidden

```
/c%3A/Users/path/to/repo     # URL-encoded
C:\c%3A\Users\path\to\repo   # duplicated drive
\c%3A\Users\path\to\repo     # leading slash + encoding
```

## Normalization (Windows)

Before calling MCP Git:

```python
def normalize_mcp_git_repo_path(path: str) -> str:
    path = path.replace("%3A", ":")
    path = path.replace("\\", "/")
    if ":" in path:
        drive, rest = path.split(":", 1)
        drive = drive.lstrip("/")
        path = f"{drive}:{rest}"
    return path
```

Example: `normalize_mcp_git_repo_path("/c%3A/Users/repo")` → `c:/Users/repo` (adjust casing to match the real drive letter).

## Usage

```python
repo_path = normalize_mcp_git_repo_path(workspace_path)
# mcp_git_git_status(repo_path=repo_path)
```

On Linux/macOS devcontainers, use the workspace absolute path with forward slashes (e.g. `/workspaces/SmartWealthAI`) — no drive letter required.

## Common mistakes

- Passing Cursor/workspace paths with `%3A` encoding.
- Mixing `\` and `/` without normalizing.
- Relative paths instead of absolute repo roots.
